 "summary": "The post-PR surface is minimal and canonical: no compatibility aliases or shims, no hidden general infrastructure (the two List identities and the unitary-trace bound are public in their upstream namespaces at mirrored paths), no exposed bodies, and `(rfl)` used for the three identification lemmas. Every definition carries its `*_def`, both directions of the dipole/quadrupole identification, and complete parallel specialisations of the general-`n` results; the `@[simp]` set is confluent on the overlapping coincidence rules and the conditional cancellation lemmas strictly decrease `n`, with `NeZero Nc` present exactly where `Nc = 0` would falsify the statement.",
